{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Paul writes to the believers in Rome
A list of names in the letter [Cm]of grace
Asyncritus and Phlegon [Cm]are known
But Hermes stands in the o[Gm]pen space
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes
Patrobas and Hermas with [Bb]care
And the [Cm]brothers who stand with them
In the circle of love that is [Gm]fair
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A Christian living in the city walls
Part of the community that he [Bb]knew
[Cm]Recognized by the apostle’s hand
His name [Cm]is written in the view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Greet Asyn[Gm]critus, Phlegon, Hermes
Patrobas and Hermas with care
And the [Bb]brothers who [Cm]stand with them
In the circle of love that is [Gm]fair
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Greet Hermes in the letter’s light
[Cm]His name is kept in the Roman [Gm]night
{end_of_verse}
